# Manual API requests. Open in VS Code with the "REST Client" extension
# and click "Send Request" above each one. Start the API first: npm run dev
# The login requests save the cookie, so later requests are logged in.
# Logins are from the README (seed data). Product IDs: check GET /products.

@api = http://localhost:3001

### Health
GET {{api}}/health

### ---------- Customer ----------

### Log in as a customer
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "alice@example.com", "password": "Customer123!" }

### Who am I?
GET {{api}}/auth/me

### Products in stock, with current prices
GET {{api}}/products

### Place an order (replace the product IDs from GET /products)
POST {{api}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "items": [{ "productId": 1, "quantity": 1 }, { "productId": 3, "quantity": 2 }] }

### My order history
GET {{api}}/orders

### Customer on an admin endpoint: expect 403
POST {{api}}/products
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Nope", "priceCents": 100 }

### Log out
POST {{api}}/auth/logout

### ---------- Admin ----------

### Log in as admin
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "admin@example.com", "password": "Admin123!" }

### All products, including sold out
GET {{api}}/products

### Create a product
POST {{api}}/products
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Webcam", "description": "1080p", "imageUrl": "/products/webcam.svg", "priceCents": 5999, "unitsInStock": 10 }

### Update a price
PATCH {{api}}/products/1/price
Content-Type: application/json

{ "priceCents": 2499 }

### Restock
POST {{api}}/products/1/stock
Content-Type: application/json

{ "quantity": 10, "reason": "RESTOCK" }

### Remove stock (e.g. damaged)
POST {{api}}/products/1/stock
Content-Type: application/json

{ "quantity": -1, "reason": "ADJUSTMENT" }
